= List of Symbols

/ $beta$: Benchmark rate of customers per day per 100 sq ft for a business type
/ $rho$: Competitor density in competitors per km#super[2]
/ $tau$: Kendall's rank correlation coefficient
/ $a$: Number of amenities within 1 km of a location
/ $b$: Transit indicator, 1 if a metro or rail stop lies within 800 m and 0 otherwise
/ $c$: Cost of goods as a share of revenue
/ $c_k$: Number of points of interest or transit stops in group $k$ inside the radius
/ $f$: Footfall multiplier
/ $g$: Competition factor
/ $m$: Customer multiplier of a revenue scenario (0.7, 1.0 or 1.3)
/ $m_(i k)$: Score of area $i$ on criterion $k$ (0 to 10)
/ $m'_(i k)$: Score of area $i$ on criterion $k$ after inverting criteria where lower is better
/ $n$: Number of competitors inside the radius or within 1 km, as stated in the text
/ $n_(500)$: Number of competitors within 500 m of a candidate spot
/ $p_"med"$: Median sale price per sq ft of nearby listings in rupees
/ $r$: Radius of the analysis in km
/ $t$: Average ticket in rupees
/ $w_k$: Weight of criterion or group $k$
/ $A$: Store area in sq ft
/ $C_k$: Saturation cap of group $k$
/ $D$: Catchment demand index (0 to 100)
/ $F$: Fixed monthly costs in rupees
/ $K$: Number of criteria
/ $N$: Customers per day
/ $O$: Opportunity score of a candidate spot
/ $P$: Monthly profit in rupees
/ $R$: Monthly rent in rupees
/ $S_i$: Weighted score of area $i$
/ $T$: Payback period in months
/ $U$: One-time setup cost in rupees
/ $V$: Monthly revenue in rupees
/ $V^*$: Break-even monthly revenue in rupees
